"""Embedded FP64-gold KDA test cases for M0 reference validation.

Generated from naive_recurrent_kda (fp64) via the kda-bench FLA venv.
Each case stores raw operator-contract inputs (un-normalised q/k, raw gate,
raw beta_logits) and the FP64 gold output + final-state computed with the
full gate/normalization pipeline.

State layout for all cases: K_FIRST [N, HV, K, V].
Tolerance: rel_err = RMSE(gold-ref)/RMSE(gold) < 1e-5 (fixed-length).
"""


# ===-----------------------------------------------------------=== #
# Case 0: K=16, V=16, N=1, HV=1,
#          H=1, T=3 (total_T=3),
#          gate_mode=original, beta_mode=logits
# ===-----------------------------------------------------------=== #


def case0_meta() -> Tuple[Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int]:
    # Returns (K, V, N, HV, H, T_per_seq, total_T)
    return (16, 16, 1, 1, 1, 3, 3)


